{
  "reason": "The phone selects the same host-owned project/workspace, local checkout and managed worktree semantics as the desktop. Git operations remain scoped to known targets; a draft identity cannot be reused for different content, and failed worktree promotions remove only their own resources. Selector lifecycle now preserves same-target drafts, removes context controls as first-send creation begins, and restores unchanged draft choices after a confirmed rejection. Unavailable repository targets force Local, and an existing managed worktree does not expose another mode or branch selector.",
